{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/946066-my-issue-with-chronicles-of-darkness","id":946066,"title":"My issue with Chronicles of Darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-08T04:11:58-07:00","id":946066,"title":"My issue with Chronicles of Darkness","content":"Chronicles of Darkness has a great setting, and the rules are better for crossovers than the old World of Darkness rules were. My issue with CoD stems from something I read on the forums: that if X is the Prince of Albuquerque in a given Vampire: the Requiem sourcebook, that is no guarantee that X will still be Prince in Changeling: the Lost, or even in the next Requiem supplement. I understand this is a toolbox supplement, but I expect an internally consistent world. I would like the Prince of Albuquerque to remain constant from one game line to the next, and if he or she doesn't, I would like an in-game explanation as to why the change occurred. What do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T04:24:13-07:00","id":946068,"title":"","content":"Does your experience with this issue stem from what you've read in the books, or just what you've heard people describe? Because I'd call that one an oversimplification. There are quite a lot of callbacks and consistency across books about particular setting details, recurring characters, and writeups that gain dimensions when taken in the context of what came before. Honestly, I don't even really use the word &quot;toolkit&quot; much when describing the CofD. It's hardly the Cortex Hacker's Guide or any other big list of recombinable modules. It has more in the way of optional modules and alternatives presented than the World of Darkness, but, well, that's a pretty relative comparison.<br /> <br /> I would say the big difference people try to put their finger on is more of the &quot;book one&quot; approach, where most CofD supplements try to be written to be useful for readers regardless of whether they have any other given supplements, just the core book of whatever gameline the supplement is for \u2013 readers for whom this is the first supplement book they read. There's an exception to every rule, of course, but setting material is usually presented in a way that's designed to make sense regardless of whether you know who Felix is or where he really came from, or how far the rabbit hole goes with the Board of Directors of the Cheiron Group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T04:25:22-07:00","id":946069,"title":"","content":"You shouldn't expect an internally consistent world.<br /> <br /> Everything present in the games are story hooks. There's no unified setting or metaplot to justify Changeling describing why something is different from Vampire","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T05:14:09-07:00","id":946085,"title":"","content":"Stupid Loserman: You are correct. I am basing my complaint on something I heard secondhand in the forums. I have read many of the first edition Requiem, Awakening and Vigil books, as well as the core book for Promethean, and enjoyed them very much. I am now trying to decide whether it is worth investing my money in the second edition CoD books. Reseru: I just wish Chronicles of Darkness would keep its fluff (which overall is really good) but be more like classic WoD with respect to internal consistency and metaplot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T05:31:52-07:00","id":946090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/946066-my-issue-with-chronicles-of-darkness?p=946085#post946085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just wish Chronicles of Darkness would keep its fluff (which overall is really good) but be more like classic WoD with respect to internal consistency and metaplot.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the thing is, a <b><i>lot</i></b> of CofD players prefer it <b><i>because</i></b> it doesn't have anything resembling a metaplot. Each game is designed with the assumption that you won't be playing major crossovers because the assumption is that you only have the core book for that game line and no others. 2E has actually been a little different about this: Tokyo is being set up as a major crossover city, and has a write-up in almost every 2E core book from the perspective of those supernaturals (though they don't talk about cross-splat interactions outside of the Beast book, and the Hototogisu shows up in a different form in each write-up).<br /> <br /> I can understand not being satisfied with that, but I personally would hate to see CofD's setting become anything more like WoD's than it is already, including internal consistency or metaplot.<br /> <br /> I also want to briefly explain why this is important to me: I play these games because they make sure that the focus is on the player characters, and setting elements tend to only be introduced as plot hooks or context. As soon as I start seeing a <i>narrative</i> show up in the books, I know that the game's no longer about the characters but instead about the world and some sort of ongoing story that I've got no influence on. Does that make sense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T05:38:15-07:00","id":946094,"title":"","content":"The reason it seems they don't have internal consistency is <i>because</i> there's no metaplot, though. The city write-ups in the second edition cores aren't canon, they're optional story hooks. There's a difference here.<br /> <br /> If you want there to be a consistent metaplot then you're better off with the classic WoD because there's a very intentional design philosophy on this end of things","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T05:41:42-07:00","id":946096,"title":"","content":"It does happen. In first edition the books don't always go into detail about setting information, or at least don't get into too much depth, but when they do its not uncommon for previous entries to be overlooked.<br /> <br /> That said it's more often a matter of perspective. The Chicago vampire domain is rather well established, with the Chicago book being one of the first made and the characters having basically a plot that is added upon throughout the books. But Chicago was created before Promethean, Changeling, Hunter, Geist, Demon and Mummy. So when you get into those books it's understandable that they might portray a different picture of it, especially if they're trying to make the place seem interesting for the supernatural. As cool as Prince Maxwell is in Chicago, Demon might be better served by having the Prince of Chicago somehow tied up in the God-Machine, Changeling as someone who has had contact with the Gentry or who has made extensive pledges with the leader of the freehold.<br /> <br /> Still, they do reference previous entries a good amount, too.<br /> <br /> In regards to metaplot, I'd like to point out that while it's not nearly as pervasive as old World of Darkness, there are some things that have changed from book to book according to the fiction. The domain of Chicago has been through changes since the original book came out, with certain major characters getting killed or deposed from their previously held social status. The werewolf community has faced some changes as well.<br /> <br /> Important to keep in mind that the more concrete the setting, the less leeway you have making changes, something necessary as the second editions roll out. Werewolf's first edition was first and foremost about acting as spirit police, while in second edition that's only an optional part of the focus on the hunt. The packs of Chicago and other areas would look very different through the lens of second edition. If the writers were forced to stick to what has already been established we wouldn't have the great improvements second edition brought.<br /> <br /> Plus there's the obvious problem of new games. It would be difficult to slip them into the world if the world wasn't malleable enough that established settings couldn't be changed.<br /> <br /> In the end I view continuity nods as Easter eggs. Dar-us the Slow-Killer being mentioned having taught a Beast his fighting style is a nice tidbit and nod to continuity and earlier books, without really turning the setting or narrative concrete one way or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-08-2016, 08:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T06:09:03-07:00","id":946110,"title":"","content":"I think this might come from a core misunderstanding - the reason it might differ between books is because there is no canonical metaplot in ChroD at all period. The Prince might not stay the same between books because The Prince isn't canonically defined in any of them. The settings are examples, and can absolutely be used in actual play, but they don't tell you what you <i>have</i> to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T07:20:10-07:00","id":946140,"title":"","content":"Metaplot and internal consistency are two different things. There is (almost) no metaplot in CoD, but generally there's internal consistency (with some exceptions).<br /> <br /> Vidal (New Orleans Prince) was mentioned in the Clanbooks. The San Francisco Mission from the clanbooks was included in new core. The New Atlantis projects from order books were included in the Seers book... The Julii and the Camarilla wings have been referenced in later books. The Cainite Heresy from Fall of the Camarilla is the origin of a Hunter Conspiracy. A roman Hunter Conspiracy was expanded in a Requiem for Rome SAS, Requiem for Rome referenced a lot of material from other books...<br /> <br /> In fact, if found more internal inconsistences in cWoD books than in CoD books: three different versions of the origin of the Baali, Huitzilopochtli in Mexico and as the Baali founder, the taking of New York by the Camarilla (two different versions, according the novels or the book), different dates for the diablerie of Lasombra Antediluvian (they even adressed this in a novel, giving a in-character explanation...).<br /> The only great inconsistency I've found in CoD books was the Moscow city for vampires: in Carthians they say the Carthian domain fell in the 70's or 80's, before the fall of Soviet Union. In Ancient Bloodlines is implied they still are there. And the origin of the Macellarius, that is changed in Requiem for Rome (I don't count the 2nd Editions changes, because they've been a kind of partial reboot). <br /> What CofD does is avoid referencing material from other books (not allways), but generally there's an internal consistency.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T07:23:54-07:00","id":946145,"title":"","content":"Nofather: I agree absolutely. What you're saying makes a lot of sense. In the long run, it doesn't matter that much. If I want to keep Maxwell as Prince of Chicago despite another book contradicting that, I can do so. If I want to make someone else Prince of Chicago, I can do that too. I use Chronicles of Darkness as a parallel alternate universe to the classic World of Darkness, and the lack of metaplot in some ways serves to make it different from the classic WoD. I have added a lot of historical background of my own (for example, I made Inanna, the founder of the Daeva clan, a former Moros who used a powerful ritual to bring herself back from the dead and came back as a vampire), and I have also found Dark Eras invaluable in developing the historical background of the Chronicles of Darkness setting. Anyway, thanks for your commentary. Really appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T11:45:42-07:00","id":946329,"title":"","content":"It's less that the books lack internal consistency and more that we're judicious about how much one book depends on or overlaps with another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T14:12:00-07:00","id":950216,"title":"","content":"If your looking for cross over consistantcy then perhaps the Crossover Chronicles book announced at Gencon will deliver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T07:05:20-07:00","id":951089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JulianMoon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/946066-my-issue-with-chronicles-of-darkness#post946066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chronicles of Darkness has a great setting, and the rules are better for crossovers than the old World of Darkness rules were. My issue with CoD stems from something I read on the forums: that if X is the Prince of Albuquerque in a given Vampire: the Requiem sourcebook, that is no guarantee that X will still be Prince in Changeling: the Lost, or even in the next Requiem supplement. I understand this is a toolbox supplement, but I expect an internally consistent world. I would like the Prince of Albuquerque to remain constant from one game line to the next, and if he or she doesn't, I would like an in-game explanation as to why the change occurred. What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Old world of darkness was consistent, but I actually would prefer CofD to even be more of a toolbox than it already is. I wish it would be written in such a ways to say the prince of Albuquerque could be this, or this, or it might make even more since if you did this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T12:53:40-07:00","id":951258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/946066-my-issue-with-chronicles-of-darkness?p=951089#post951089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Old world of darkness was consistent</div> </div> </div> </div>Hah! Nope. If we go setting wise? There's like a dozen ways to explain the setting differently, which is changed consistently (perhaps the only consistent thing across the board) with every new edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T05:58:40-07:00","id":951629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/946066-my-issue-with-chronicles-of-darkness?p=951258#post951258\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hah! Nope. If we go setting wise? There's like a dozen ways to explain the setting differently, which is changed consistently (perhaps the only consistent thing across the board) with every new edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>It tried though. There was a meta plot. The prince of Chicago was the prince Chicago unless someone else took over, ect. Just going on what I have been told over and over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T06:12:56-07:00","id":951636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/946066-my-issue-with-chronicles-of-darkness?p=951629#post951629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It tried though. There was a meta plot. The prince of Chicago was the prince Chicago unless someone else took over, ect. Just going on what I have been told over and over.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except not really. As early as the first few Vampire books, Lodin was Prince of Chicago unless he wasn't - having been killed by lupine or whatever. He ruled unless Modius Prince of Gary had made inroads and Lodins brood were all squabbling to pick up the pieces in his wake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T05:59:10-07:00","id":952452,"title":"","content":"We mostly haven't done things like change Princes around. There are a few places where mid-to-late 1e books contradict early 1e books, but by and large Maxwell is always Prince of Chicago.<br /> <br /> For some specifics, New Orleans is the only place in <i>Vampire</i> 1e that changed with an unfolding story. The clanbooks suggested that it was really shaken up by Hurricane Katrina. But Vidal is still the Prince, as you'll see in <i>Secrets of the Covenants</i>. Chicago had its own story in the novels and chapter fiction, but 1e didn't change its official writeup, and even in the fiction, the hierarchy is fairly consistent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}